  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tuvaluan healthcare system faces significant challenges due to strained resources and supply chains, inadequate infrastructure and shortages of qualified staff. Australia is supporting Tuvalu&#x2019;s Ministry of Health through the provision of paediatric and internal medicine specialists to Princess Margaret Hospital (PMH) in Funafuti through the Pacific Community (SPC). For the period July &#x2013; December 2024, there were a total of four specialists deployed to PMH through SPC. The paediatric specialists saw 164 patients in this period, with an average of 55 patients per month. 122 paediatric patients were seen by the internal medicine specialists, with an average of 41 per month. As well as direct clinical care, the specialists have strengthened the Tuvaluan health system&#x2019;s capacity through activities such as providing training in echocardiography, conducting audits on paediatric mortality, and developing strategies to address significant health issues such as hepatitis B.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
